{"id":"54bffd3ac2a10ea1abbf066ba702ea44ab9624b6","axis":"silent","repo":"TryGhost/Ghost","sha":"54bffd3ac2a10ea1abbf066ba702ea44ab9624b6","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/plans/better-auth-migration.md","lines":["@@ -270,19 +270,27 @@ the session (Phase 2), so they create a Better Auth session directly."," **`ghostStaffLifecycle`** (Phase 2). Ghost's status rules layered on Better"," Auth core."," ","-- Before `/sign-in/email`: `locked` sends the reset email and throws","-  `PASSWORD_RESET_REQUIRED`; `inactive` throws `ACCOUNT_SUSPENDED`; unknown","-  email and wrong password map to today's messages (§5.3).","+- `/sign-in/email` does not enumerate staff (§5.3): an unknown email and a","+  wrong password are both `INVALID_EMAIL_OR_PASSWORD`. A failed attempt for a","+  `locked` user still sends the reset email, without changing the response."," - Before magic-link, passkey and SSO sign-in: refuse `inactive`, and set a","   `locked` user's `status` to `active` (as reset does today). This runs before","-  the session is created, so the session guard below admits them.","-- After every sign-in: set `last_seen`, set `status` to `active`.","+  the session is created, so the session guard below admits them. The unlock","+  only matches a `locked` user, and a user suspended in the meantime is refused.","+- A successful `/reset-password` sets a `locked` user `active`, as legacy","+  `doReset` does, so the user can sign in afterwards (step 8, PLA-620). Until","+  then a native reset leaves the user locked.","+- After every sign-in: set `last_seen`, and set a `warn-*` status to `active`.","+  Both are bookkeeping, so a failure is logged and the sign-in stands."," - `databaseHooks.session.create.before`: refuse non-active users on every path.","   It runs after the before-hooks above, so only users still non-active by then","   are refused."," - Server-only: `setupOwner`, `acceptInvitation` (user + credential account +","-  role in one transaction), `createVerifiedSession`, `revokeUserSessions`,","-  `revokeAllSessions`, `lockAllUsers`.","+  role in one transaction), `createVerifiedSession` (the admin origin is","+  required, since a session without one is anonymous), `revokeUserSessions`,","+  `revokeAllSessions`. Authentication reset keeps legacy `lockAll`, which","+  locks users and replaces their credentials in the same transaction as the","+  key rotation and audit row, and calls `revokeAllSessions` after the commit."," "," **`ghostDeviceVerification`** (Phase 3). `twoFactor` and `emailOTP` are per-user"," opt-in; Ghost's rule is \"every staff user, trusted browser, satisfied by any","@@ -564,19 +572,26 @@ compatibility."," Compatibility controllers map Better Auth `APIError`s to `@tryghost/errors`"," with today's messages, so older Admin builds keep working:"," ","-| Better Auth                              | Ghost error                                                          |","-| ---------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |","-| `USER_NOT_FOUND`                         | `NotFoundError` `There is no user with that email address.`          |","-| `INVALID_EMAIL_OR_PASSWORD` (known user) | `ValidationError` `PASSWORD_INCORRECT` `Your password is incorrect.` |","-| `PASSWORD_RESET_REQUIRED`                | `PasswordResetRequiredError`                                         |","-| `ACCOUNT_SUSPENDED`                      | `NoPermissionError` `This account has been suspended.`               |","-| `DEVICE_VERIFICATION_REQUIRED`           | `NoPermissionError`, `Needs2FAError`, `2FA_*` code                   |","-| `INVALID_TOKEN` / expired                | existing reset-token messages                                        |","-| `TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`                      | `TooManyRequestsError`                                               |","-","-The native endpoints emit the codes the React `AuthClient` already expects","-(`USER_NOT_FOUND`, `INVALID_PASSWORD`, `PASSWORD_RESET_REQUIRED`,","-`INVALID_CODE`, `twoFactorRedirect` + `twoFactorReason`).","+| Better Auth                    | Ghost error                                                 |","+| ------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------- |","+| `INVALID_EMAIL_OR_PASSWORD`    | today's messages or one generic message, decided with SC-90 |","+| `PASSWORD_RESET_REQUIRED`      | `PasswordResetRequiredError`                                |","+| `ACCOUNT_SUSPENDED`            | `NoPermissionError` `This account has been suspended.`      |","+| `DEVICE_VERIFICATION_REQUIRED` | `NoPermissionError`, `Needs2FAError`, `2FA_*` code          |","+| `INVALID_TOKEN` / expired      | existing reset-token messages                               |","+| `TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`            | `TooManyRequestsError`                                      |","+","+The native endpoints emit the codes the React `AuthClient` expects","+(`PASSWORD_RESET_REQUIRED`, `INVALID_CODE`, `twoFactorRedirect` +","+`twoFactorReason`), except that sign-in does not enumerate staff: an unknown","+email, a wrong password and a wrong password on a suspended account are all","+Better Auth's `INVALID_EMAIL_OR_PASSWORD`, so `USER_NOT_FOUND` and","+`INVALID_PASSWORD` are not used. Admin's sign-in form keys on those two codes","+to mark the email or password field, so its native client must treat","+`INVALID_EMAIL_OR_PASSWORD` as one error for both fields. Suspension and","+`PASSWORD_RESET_REQUIRED` only show after a matching password. Today's","+messages enumerate staff (SC-90); whether the compatibility controllers keep","+them is decided with SC-90."," "," ### 5.4 Behaviour"," ","@@ -681,7 +696,9 @@ Exit: merged to main; full e2e API suite green under `legacy`.","    Until 7.0 drops `sessions`, both also delete the user's legacy `sessions`","    rows, so a rollback (§8) cannot revive a session a security event revoked."," 8. `PUT /users/password` and `PUT /authentication/password_reset` use","-   `createVerifiedSession`.","+   `createVerifiedSession`. `ghostStaffLifecycle` sets a `locked` user","+   `active` on a successful `/reset-password`, or `createVerifiedSession`","+   refuses the user it just reset."," 9. Cleanup job (§4.6)."," 10. Run `session`, `session-invalidation`, `users`, `api-tokens`,","     `key-authentication`, `sso` e2e API tests and `e2e/tests/admin/signin.test.ts`"],"additions":38,"deletions":21,"truncated":false},{"path":"ghost/core/server/auth/better-auth/README.md","lines":["@@ -60,6 +60,29 @@ until Phase 4.","   outside `server/services`, so the","   [service checks](../../services/README.md#roots-outside-this-directory) do","   not apply to it.","+- `plugins/staff-lifecycle.ts`: `ghostStaffLifecycle`, Ghost's staff status","+  rules (plan §3.3). `/sign-in/email` keeps Better Auth's","+  `INVALID_EMAIL_OR_PASSWORD` for an unknown email, a wrong password and a","+  wrong password on a suspended account, so it can't enumerate staff (unlike","+  legacy sign-in, SC-90). A `session.create.before` hook refuses non-active","+  users on every path, so a matching password on a `locked` account is","+  `PASSWORD_RESET_REQUIRED` and on an `inactive` one `ACCOUNT_SUSPENDED`;","+  magic-link, passkey and SSO sign-in instead set a `locked` user `active`.","+  Any failed password sign-in for a `locked` user emails the legacy reset","+  link, as legacy sign-in does, without awaiting it or changing the response.","+  The after-hook that does this runs after the endpoint's CSRF check, so a","+  cross-origin request sends nothing. Every new session sets `last_seen` and","+  moves a `warn-*` status to `active`; a lock or suspension committed after","+  the guard's read stands, and a failure is logged without failing sign-in.","+  The guard reads the status without a lock, so a suspension that commits","+  while a session is being created can leave a session row, which","+  `revokeUserSessions` in the same gap misses. Anything that trusts a session","+  or token (the Admin API resolver, revocation, app tokens) must check the","+  user's status too. Server-only: `createVerifiedSession`, which requires the","+  admin origin, `revokeUserSessions` and `revokeAllSessions`, which no Ghost","+  caller uses yet.","+- `routes.ts`: the Better Auth paths that matchers, limiters and","+  `disabledPaths` refer to. A mistyped path matches nothing, silently."," "," Ghost mounts at the subdirectory, so on a subdirectory install requests reach"," Better Auth as `/blog/ghost/api/admin/auth/...`. `basePath` therefore carries"],"additions":23,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"ghost/core/server/auth/better-auth/create-auth.ts","lines":["@@ -7,6 +7,8 @@ import type { Knex } from 'knex';"," import { CLIENT_IP_HEADER } from './client-ip';"," import { createKnexAdapter } from './knex-adapter';"," import { rateLimitStorage, type Limiters } from './rate-limit';","+import { ghostStaffLifecycle } from './plugins/staff-lifecycle';","+import { ROUTES } from './routes';"," import {","   generateGhostId,","   ghostCreateDefaults,","@@ -37,6 +39,8 @@ export type CreateAuthDeps = {","   logger: Logger;","   /** Ghost's `spam` limiters, which also back the compatibility routes */","   limiters: Limiters;","+  /** Emails a legacy password reset link; a locked user's sign-in sends one */","+  sendPasswordResetEmail(email: string): Promise<void>;"," };"," "," /**","@@ -73,6 +77,8 @@ export function assertDatabaseSupported({","   }"," }"," ","+const CLEARS_FAILED_SIGN_INS: string[] = [ROUTES.signInEmail, ROUTES.resetPassword];","+"," const isPlainObject = (value: unknown): value is Record<string, unknown> =>","   typeof value === 'object' && value !== null && Object.getPrototypeOf(value) === Object.prototype;"," ","@@ -160,11 +166,11 @@ export function createAuth(deps: CreateAuthDeps) {","     // On by default in production only","     rateLimit: { enabled: true, customStorage: rateLimitStorage(deps.limiters) },","     disabledPaths: [","-      '/sign-up/email',","-      '/update-user',","-      '/change-email',","-      '/delete-user',","-      '/sign-in/social',","+      ROUTES.signUpEmail,","+      ROUTES.updateUser,","+      ROUTES.changeEmail,","+      ROUTES.deleteUser,","+      ROUTES.signInSocial,","     ],","     hooks: {","       after: createAuthMiddleware(async (ctx) => {","@@ -175,7 +181,7 @@ export function createAuth(deps: CreateAuthDeps) {","         const returned = ctx.context.returned;"," ","         // Clears this IP's failed sign-ins, as the compatibility routes do","-        if (['/sign-in/email', '/reset-password'].includes(ctx.path) && !isAPIError(returned)) {","+        if (CLEARS_FAILED_SIGN_INS.includes(ctx.path) && !isAPIError(returned)) {","           const ip = ctx.request.headers.get(CLIENT_IP_HEADER) ?? undefined;","           // Awaited, so the next request sees the cleared count","           await deps.limiters","@@ -189,6 +195,7 @@ export function createAuth(deps: CreateAuthDeps) {","         }","       }),","     },","+    plugins: [ghostStaffLifecycle({ sendPasswordResetEmail: deps.sendPasswordResetEmail })],","     telemetry: { enabled: false },","     logger: {","       log: (level, message, ...args) => deps.logger[level](message, ...args),"],"additions":13,"deletions":6,"truncated":false},{"path":"ghost/core/server/auth/better-auth/index.ts","lines":["@@ -33,6 +33,13 @@ export default defineService('Better Auth', async (): Promise<GhostAuth> => {","       userLogin: spamPrevention.userLogin,","       userReset: spamPrevention.userReset,","     },","+    // The legacy reset email and token, until the reset flow moves (plan Phase 2)","+    async sendPasswordResetEmail(email) {","+      const passwordreset = require('../passwordreset').default;","+      const api = require('../../api').endpoints;","+      const token = await passwordreset.generateToken(email, api.settings);","+      await passwordreset.sendResetNotification(token, api.mail);","+    },","   });","   // betterAuth() defers its setup to this promise; awaiting it fails boot, not the first request","   await auth.$context;"],"additions":7,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"ghost/core/server/auth/better-auth/plugins/staff-lifecycle.ts","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,202 @@","+import { runWithTransaction } from '@better-auth/core/context';","+import { APIError, BASE_ERROR_CODES, defineErrorCodes, getCurrentAdapter } from 'better-auth';","+import type { AuthContext, BetterAuthPlugin, User } from 'better-auth';","+import { createAuthEndpoint, createAuthMiddleware, isAPIError } from 'better-auth/api';","+import { setSessionCookie } from 'better-auth/cookies';","+import { z } from 'zod';","+import { ROUTES, SSO_PREFIX } from '../routes';","+","+// Legacy user model statuses; `warn-*` users can still sign in","+const WARN_STATUSES = ['warn-1', 'warn-2', 'warn-3', 'warn-4'];","+const ACTIVE_STATUSES = ['active', ...WARN_STATUSES];","+","+export const isActiveStatus = (status: unknown): boolean =>","+  typeof status === 'string' && ACTIVE_STATUSES.includes(status);","+","+/**","+ * Only shown once the user is known: after a matching password, or on a path","+ * that already proved who they are. An unknown email and a wrong password","+ * both stay Better Auth's `INVALID_EMAIL_OR_PASSWORD`, so sign-in can't","+ * enumerate staff (plan §5.3).","+ */","+export const STAFF_LIFECYCLE_ERROR_CODES = defineErrorCodes({","+  PASSWORD_RESET_REQUIRED:","+    'For security, you need to create a new password. An email has been sent to you with instructions!',","+  ACCOUNT_SUSPENDED: 'Your account was suspended.',","+});","+","+const ERRORS = STAFF_LIFECYCLE_ERROR_CODES;","+","+// Sign-in methods that prove control of the account without its password, so","+// they unlock a locked user as a password reset does","+const PASSWORDLESS_SIGN_IN: string[] = [ROUTES.magicLinkVerify, ROUTES.passkeyVerifyAuthentication];","+","+const isPasswordlessSignIn = (path: string | undefined) =>","+  !!path && (PASSWORDLESS_SIGN_IN.includes(path) || path.startsWith(SSO_PREFIX));","+","+type StaffUser = User & { status?: string | null };","+","+export type StaffLifecycleOptions = {","+  /** Emails a password reset link, as the legacy session endpoint does for a locked user */","+  sendPasswordResetEmail(email: string): Promise<void>;","+};","+","+const refusal = (status: unknown) =>","+  status === 'locked'","+    ? APIError.from('UNAUTHORIZED', ERRORS.PASSWORD_RESET_REQUIRED)","+    : APIError.from('FORBIDDEN', ERRORS.ACCOUNT_SUSPENDED);","+","+/** Ghost's staff status rules on top of Better Auth core (plan §3.3). */","+export const ghostStaffLifecycle = (options: StaffLifecycleOptions) => {","+  let authContext: AuthContext;","+","+  // Matches the status read earlier, so a lock or suspension committed since stands","+  const setStatus = async (userId: string, from: string[], to: string): Promise<number> => {","+    const adapter = await getCurrentAdapter(authContext.adapter);","+    return adapter.updateMany({","+      model: 'user',","+      where: [","+        { field: 'id', value: userId },","+        { field: 'status', operator: 'in', value: from },","+      ],","+      update: { status: to },","+    });","+  };","+","+  return {","+    id: 'ghost-staff-lifecycle',","+    $ERROR_CODES: STAFF_LIFECYCLE_ERROR_CODES,","+","+    init(ctx) {","+      authContext = ctx;","+      return {","+        options: {","+          databaseHooks: {","+            session: {","+              create: {","+                // Every path that creates a session, including server-only ones","+                async before(session, endpoint) {","+                  const adapter = await getCurrentAdapter(authContext.adapter);","+                  const user = await adapter.findOne<StaffUser>({","+                    model: 'user',","+                    where: [{ field: 'id', value: session.userId }],","+                  });","+                  if (!user) {","+                    throw APIError.from('NOT_FOUND', BASE_ERROR_CODES.USER_NOT_FOUND);","+                  }","+                  if (isActiveStatus(user.status)) {","+                    return;","+                  }","+                  if (user.status === 'locked' && isPasswordlessSignIn(endpoint?.path)) {","+                    // No match means the user was suspended since the read","+                    if (await setStatus(user.id, ['locked'], 'active')) {","+                      return;","+                    }","+                    throw refusal('inactive');","+                  }","+                  throw refusal(user.status);","+                },","+                // Bookkeeping only: the session exists by now, so a failure is logged, not thrown","+                async after(session) {","+                  if (!session) {","+                    return;","+                  }","+                  try {","+                    const adapter = await getCurrentAdapter(authContext.adapter);","+                    await adapter.update({","+                      model: 'user',","+                      where: [{ field: 'id', value: session.userId }],","+                      update: { last_seen: new Date() },","+                    });","+                    await setStatus(session.userId, WARN_STATUSES, 'active');","+                  } catch (err) {","+                    authContext.logger.error('Updating the user after sign-in failed', err);","+                  }","+                },","+              },","+            },","+          },","+        },","+      };","+    },","+","+    hooks: {","+      // After the endpoint, so its CSRF check and validation have run","+      after: [","+        {","+          matcher: (ctx) => ctx.path === ROUTES.signInEmail,","+          handler: createAuthMiddleware(async (ctx) => {","+            const returned = ctx.context.returned;","+            if (!isAPIError(returned)) {","+              return;","+            }","+            const code = returned.body?.code;","+            if (","+              code !== ERRORS.PASSWORD_RESET_REQUIRED.code &&","+              code !== BASE_ERROR_CODES.INVALID_EMAIL_OR_PASSWORD.code","+            ) {","+              return;","+            }","+","+            // A locked user's password was replaced, so as in legacy sign-in","+            // any attempt emails a reset link. The response stays as it is, and","+            // the email isn't awaited, so neither reveals the status","+            const found = await ctx.context.internalAdapter.findUserByEmail(ctx.body.email);","+            if (found && 'status' in found.user && found.user.status === 'locked') {","+              options","+                .sendPasswordResetEmail(found.user.email)","+                .catch((err: unknown) =>","+                  ctx.context.logger.error('Password reset email failed', err),","+                );","+            }","+          }),","+        },","+      ],","+    },","+","+    endpoints: {","+      /** A verified session with its cookie, for flows that already proved the user (plan §5.1) */","+      createVerifiedSession: createAuthEndpoint.serverOnly(","+        {","+          method: 'POST',","+          body: z.object({","+            userId: z.string(),","+            origin: z.string(),","+          }),","+        },","+        async (ctx) => {","+          const { userId, origin } = ctx.body;","+          const user = await ctx.context.internalAdapter.findUserById(userId);","+          if (!user) {","+            throw APIError.from('NOT_FOUND', BASE_ERROR_CODES.USER_NOT_FOUND);","+          }","+          // Hooks join the transaction; overrideAll keeps `verified` from its default","+          const session = await runWithTransaction(ctx.context.adapter, () =>","+            ctx.context.internalAdapter.createSession(","+              userId,","+              false,","+              { verified: true, origin },","+              true,","+            ),","+          );","+          await setSessionCookie(ctx, { session, user });","+          return ctx.json({ session, user });","+        },","+      ),","+","+      revokeUserSessions: createAuthEndpoint.serverOnly(","+        { method: 'POST', body: z.object({ userId: z.string() }) },","+        async (ctx) => {","+          await ctx.context.internalAdapter.deleteUserSessions(ctx.body.userId);","+          return ctx.json({ status: true });","+        },","+      ),","+","+      revokeAllSessions: createAuthEndpoint.serverOnly({ method: 'POST' }, async (ctx) => {","+        const adapter = await getCurrentAdapter(ctx.context.adapter);","+        const count = await adapter.deleteMany({ model: 'session', where: [] });","+        return ctx.json({ count });","+      }),","+    },","+  } satisfies BetterAuthPlugin;","+};"],"additions":202,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"ghost/core/server/auth/better-auth/rate-limit.ts","lines":["@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@"," import type { BetterAuthRateLimitOptions } from 'better-auth';","+import { ROUTES } from './routes';"," "," type RateLimitStorage = NonNullable<BetterAuthRateLimitOptions['customStorage']>;"," ","@@ -25,16 +26,16 @@ const PASSWORD_RESET = '/authentication/password_reset/';"," // Each native credential route counts against its compatibility route's limiters"," const ROUTE_LIMITERS: Record<string, { route: string; limiters: LimiterName[] }> = {","   // POST /session","-  '/sign-in/email': { route: SESSION, limiters: ['globalBlock', 'userLogin'] },","+  [ROUTES.signInEmail]: { route: SESSION, limiters: ['globalBlock', 'userLogin'] },","   // Sends an email per request, like POST /authentication/password_reset","-  '/sign-in/magic-link': { route: PASSWORD_RESET, limiters: ['globalReset', 'userReset'] },","+  [ROUTES.signInMagicLink]: { route: PASSWORD_RESET, limiters: ['globalReset', 'userReset'] },","   // POST /authentication/password_reset","-  '/request-password-reset': { route: PASSWORD_RESET, limiters: ['globalReset', 'userReset'] },","+  [ROUTES.requestPasswordReset]: { route: PASSWORD_RESET, limiters: ['globalReset', 'userReset'] },","   // PUT /authentication/password_reset","-  '/reset-password': { route: PASSWORD_RESET, limiters: ['globalBlock'] },","+  [ROUTES.resetPassword]: { route: PASSWORD_RESET, limiters: ['globalBlock'] },","   // Check the current password; PUT /users/password has no limit, so these get their own","-  '/change-password': { route: '/change-password', limiters: ['globalBlock'] },","-  '/verify-password': { route: '/verify-password', limiters: ['globalBlock'] },","+  [ROUTES.changePassword]: { route: ROUTES.changePassword, limiters: ['globalBlock'] },","+  [ROUTES.verifyPassword]: { route: ROUTES.verifyPassword, limiters: ['globalBlock'] },"," };"," "," // Their Express middleware keys these on `req.path`, as Admin calls it"],"additions":7,"deletions":6,"truncated":false},{"path":"ghost/core/server/auth/better-auth/routes.ts","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@","+/**","+ * Better Auth endpoint paths Ghost refers to, relative to `basePath`. A","+ * mistyped path never matches and fails silently, so every matcher, limiter","+ * and disabled path reads them from here. Plugin paths are listed ahead of","+ * the plugins that serve them.","+ */","+export const ROUTES = {","+  signInEmail: '/sign-in/email',","+  signInSocial: '/sign-in/social',","+  signUpEmail: '/sign-up/email',","+  updateUser: '/update-user',","+  changeEmail: '/change-email',","+  deleteUser: '/delete-user',","+  changePassword: '/change-password',","+  verifyPassword: '/verify-password',","+  requestPasswordReset: '/request-password-reset',","+  resetPassword: '/reset-password',","+  // magicLink plugin","+  signInMagicLink: '/sign-in/magic-link',","+  magicLinkVerify: '/magic-link/verify',","+  // passkey plugin","+  passkeyVerifyAuthentication: '/passkey/verify-authentication',","+} as const;","+","+/** `@better-auth/sso` callback paths, which carry a provider id */","+export const SSO_PREFIX = '/sso/';"],"additions":26,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"ghost/package.json","lines":["@@ -76,6 +76,7 @@","   },","   \"dependencies\": {","     \"@aws-sdk/client-s3\": \"3.1161.0\",","+    \"@better-auth/core\": \"catalog:\",","     \"@breejs/later\": \"catalog:\",","     \"@extractus/oembed-extractor\": \"catalog:\",","     \"@faker-js/faker\": \"catalog:\","],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"ghost/test/e2e-api/admin/credential-passwords.test.ts","lines":["@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@ function betterAuth() {","     password: security.password,","     logger: { debug() {}, info() {}, warn() {}, error() {} },","     limiters: { globalBlock: allow, globalReset: allow, userLogin: allow, userReset: allow },","+    sendPasswordResetEmail: async () => {},","   });","   const origin = urlUtils.getAdminOrigin();"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"ghost/test/e2e-server/better-auth-staff-lifecycle.isolated.test.ts","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,180 @@","+import assert from 'node:assert/strict';","+import sinon from 'sinon';","+import request from 'supertest';","+const {","+  startGhost,","+  fixtureManager,","+  configUtils,","+  mockManager,","+  resetRateLimits,","+} = require('../utils/e2e-framework');","+const auth = require('../../core/server/auth');","+const db = require('../../core/server/data/db');","+const jobsService = require('../../core/server/services/jobs-service');","+const stripe = require('../../core/server/services/stripe');","+const sentry = require('../../core/shared/sentry');","+const DataGenerator = require('../utils/fixtures/data-generator');","+","+const isSQLite = ['sqlite3', 'better-sqlite3'].includes(db.knex.client.config.client);","+","+const [owner, locked, inactive] = DataGenerator.Content.users;","+","+// Native sign-in and the server-only helpers under ghostStaffLifecycle","+describe.skipIf(isSQLite)('ghostStaffLifecycle under auth:engine better-auth', function () {","+  const sandbox = sinon.createSandbox();","+  const adminOrigin = 'http://localhost:2369';","+  const host = new URL(adminOrigin).host;","+  let app: Parameters<typeof request>[0];","+  let mail: ReturnType<typeof mockManager.mockMail>;","+","+  const signIn = (email: string, password: string) =>","+    request(app)","+      .post('/ghost/api/admin/auth/sign-in/email')","+      .set('Host', host)","+      .set('Origin', adminOrigin)","+      .send({ email, password });","+","+  const userRow = (id: string) => db.knex('users').where({ id }).first();","+  const sessionCount = async (userId?: string) => {","+    const query = db.knex('user_sessions');","+    if (userId) {","+      query.where({ user_id: userId });","+    }","+    const [{ count }] = await query.count({ count: '*' });","+    return Number(count);","+  };","+  const api = () => auth.betterAuth.service.api;","+","+  beforeAll(async function () {","+    configUtils.set('sentry:disabled', true);","+    sandbox.stub(sentry, 'captureException');","+    sandbox.stub(sentry, 'captureMessage');","+    configUtils.set('auth:engine', 'better-auth');","+    configUtils.set('createInDevelopmentTables', true);","+    configUtils.set('url', `${adminOrigin}/`);","+","+    app = await startGhost({ backend: true, frontend: false, server: false });","+    await fixtureManager.init('users');","+  });","+","+  beforeEach(async function () {","+    await resetRateLimits();","+    await db.knex('user_sessions').del();","+    await db.knex('users').update({ status: 'active', last_seen: null });","+    await db.knex('users').where({ id: locked.id }).update({ status: 'locked' });","+    await db.knex('users').where({ id: inactive.id }).update({ status: 'inactive' });","+    mail = mockManager.mockMail();","+  });","+","+  afterEach(function () {","+    mockManager.restore();","+  });","+","+  afterAll(async function () {","+    sandbox.restore();","+    try {","+      await jobsService.shutdown();","+    } finally {","+      await stripe.shutdown();","+      await configUtils.restore();","+    }","+  });","+","+  describe('native sign-in', function () {","+    it('signs in an active user and records last_seen', async function () {","+      const response = await signIn(owner.email, owner.password).expect(200);","+","+      assert.match([response.headers['set-cookie']].flat().join(), /ghost-admin-api-session=/);","+      assert.equal(await sessionCount(owner.id), 1);","+      const user = await userRow(owner.id);","+      assert.equal(user.status, 'active');","+      assert.ok(user.last_seen);","+    });","+","+    it('refuses a locked user whose password matches and emails a reset link', async function () {","+      const response = await signIn(locked.email, locked.password).expect(401);","+","+      assert.equal(response.body.code, 'PASSWORD_RESET_REQUIRED');","+      assert.equal(await sessionCount(locked.id), 0);","+      assert.equal((await userRow(locked.id)).status, 'locked');","+      const sent = await mockManager.assert.sentEmailEventually({ to: locked.email });","+      assert.match(sent.html, /\\/ghost\\/reset\\//);","+    });","+","+    it('emails a locked user a reset link on a wrong password, with the generic error', async function () {","+      const response = await signIn(locked.email, 'not-the-password').expect(401);","+","+      assert.equal(response.body.code, 'INVALID_EMAIL_OR_PASSWORD');","+      await mockManager.assert.sentEmailEventually({ to: locked.email });","+    });","+","+    it('refuses a suspended user whose password matches', async function () {","+      const response = await signIn(inactive.email, inactive.password).expect(403);","+","+      assert.equal(response.body.code, 'ACCOUNT_SUSPENDED');","+      assert.equal(response.body.message, 'Your account was suspended.');","+      assert.equal(await sessionCount(inactive.id), 0);","+      mail.assertSentEmailCount(0);","+    });","+","+    it('answers an unknown email, a wrong password and a suspended user alike', async function () {","+      const unknown = await signIn('nobody@example.com', owner.password).expect(401);","+      const wrong = await signIn(owner.email, 'not-the-password').expect(401);","+      const suspended = await signIn(inactive.email, 'not-the-password').expect(401);","+","+      assert.equal(unknown.body.code, 'INVALID_EMAIL_OR_PASSWORD');","+      assert.deepEqual(wrong.body, unknown.body);","+      assert.deepEqual(suspended.body, unknown.body);","+      assert.equal((await userRow(owner.id)).last_seen, null);","+      mail.assertSentEmailCount(0);","+    });","+","+    it('looks nothing up for a cross-origin request', async function () {","+      const response = await request(app)","+        .post('/ghost/api/admin/auth/sign-in/email')","+        .set('Host', host)","+        .set('Origin', 'http://elsewhere.example')","+        .send({ email: locked.email, password: locked.password })","+        .expect(403);","+","+      assert.equal(response.body.code, 'INVALID_ORIGIN');","+      mail.assertSentEmailCount(0);","+    });","+  });","+","+  describe('server-only helpers', function () {","+    it('creates a verified session with its cookie', async function () {","+      const { headers } = await api().createVerifiedSession({","+        body: { userId: owner.id, origin: adminOrigin },","+        returnHeaders: true,","+      });","+","+      const session = await db.knex('user_sessions').where({ user_id: owner.id }).first();"],"additions":152,"deletions":0,"truncated":false}],"additions":470,"deletions":33,"truncated":true,"file_count":10},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-11-18T16:50:24.702772+00:00"}